Step-by-step execution
Step 1 — Create the experiment files
Inside your GitHub repository, select Add file → Create new file and add the five files under:

Experiment-06-DCGAN-Image-Synthesis/
Step 2 — Set up Python
Open the experiment folder in VS Code.

Create a virtual environment:

python -m venv .venv



Activate it on Windows PowerShell:

.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1



Step 3 — Install dependencies

python -m pip install --upgrade pip
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt



Step 4 — Run the experiment

python dcgan.py



The first run downloads MNIST if it is not cached. The program trains the DCGAN for 20 epochs and saves generated images and model files.

Training may be slow on a CPU. For a quick test, you can temporarily set EPOCHS = 1 and then restore EPOCHS = 20 for full training.

Note: With EPOCHS = 1, only generated_epoch_01.png and the final output images will be created. The other epoch-specific images require their corresponding epochs.
